WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.950
Treasure Island

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.680
<i>Old Redruth is dead.</i>

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:24.960
<i>One of Silver's men...</i>

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.440
<i>...killed old Redruth without hesitation.</i>

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:32.260
<i>Among our allies on the journey
from Black Hill to Treasure Island,</i>

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:34.130
<i>he was the first victim.</i>

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:42.380
<i>Even I, who dreamt of Treasure Island,</i>

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:44.480
<i>have begun to open my eyes.</i>

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:48.380
<i>This isn't the fabulous adventure that I had dreamt about.</i>

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:51.320
<i>It's not just fun every day!</i>

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.990
<i>Go ahead.
Shoot if you want to.</i>

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.180
<i>Mom...</i>

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:06.900
<i>I hate Silver!
I'll never forgive him!</i>

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.300
<i>He betrayed me.
He betrayed us all!</i>

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:13.420
<i>Silver's even gone as far as to kill old Redruth!</i>

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:16.460
<i>Mother, I'll fight against Silver!</i>

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:18.580
<i>The treasure doesn't matter anymore!</i>

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:22.250
<i>Now, he's asked for it.
Between Silver and I, it's war!</i>

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.960
Treasure
Island

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:29.760
Takarajima

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.570
saa ikou

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.570
Come, let's go

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.660
yume ni mita shima heto

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.660
To the island that I've dreamed of

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:45.500
nami wo koete kaze ni notte

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:45.500
Across the waves, on the wind

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:48.380
umi hedeyou

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:48.380
We'll travel the oceans

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:51.300
ikute ni wa

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:51.300
Many of us

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:54.300
minna mada shiranai

00:01:51.550 --> 00:01:54.300
Still don't know of

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:58.050
fushigi na hiru to yoru toga

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:58.050
The days and nights full of mystery

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.550
matte iru darou

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.550
That await us there

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:04.060
itsumo shinji you

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:04.060
We must always have trust

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.310
magokoro wo

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.310
And be sincere

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:13.570
yuuki wo mune ni susumou yo

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:13.570
And have courage in our hearts to move forward

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:16.700
tade hitotsu no

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:16.700
I only...

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:20.120
akogare dake wa

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:20.120
...have one desire

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:22.410
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:22.410
And no one...

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:29.120
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:29.120
...will ever take it away

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:35.670
tade hitotsu no

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:35.670
I only...

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.970
akogare dake wa

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.970
...have one desire

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:41.300
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:41.300
And no one...

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:48.230
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:48.230
...will ever take it away

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:59.320
episode

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:59.320
Allies vs. Enemies,
\h           That's Life!

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:03.200
<i>I don't know what to do...</i>

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:08.720
<i>We should never have let them take refuge in the fort.</i>

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:12.060
<i>Judging by their inferior numbers,</i>

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:15.140
<i>I thought that they'd surrender under our threats,</i>

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:16.880
<i>but they held up well.</i>

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:21.140
<i>But now, we have a more pressing concern.</i>

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:22.840
<i>This cursed fever.</i>

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:27.100
Hey, Puppy, how's Anderson?

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:30.060
Not good.
His fever hasn't gone down.

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:37.040
<i>At the fort, they have a roof over their heads.</i>

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:41.780
<i>But for us, who sleep here, the chance of catching this fever is high.</i>

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.420
<i>Only three are ill,</i>

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:45.990
<i>but if this continues, we'll all catch it.</i>

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:48.950
<i>And then, it will be too late.</i>

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:54.580
<i>We must act while we're still healthy.</i>

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.820
<i>Even though we have greater numbers,</i>

00:03:56.820 --> 00:03:58.920
<i>I still have fewer men to rely on.</i>

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:03.170
<i>I'll have to be cunning.</i>

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:38.500
Jim, you must sleep a little.
You didn't sleep at all last night.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:40.130
I don't need any sleep!

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:00.690
I don't need any sleep!
None at all!

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:16.610
Old Redruth...

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:25.090
It's Silver!
He's coming this way!

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:38.440
He has a white flag!
Silver has a white flag!

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:40.900
What?
A white flag?

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:45.120
I have the parliamentary flag!
I'm here to talk!

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:47.660
Let me in!

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:51.540
Why do you suddenly feel like talking?!
 We have nothing to say to you!

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:54.100
I'm going to shoot this pirate!

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:55.710
Wait, Mr. Trelawney!

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:58.670
Let's hear what he has to say before we act.

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:01.820
But, captain, what if it's a trap?

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:03.630
I don't think so, Trelawney.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.820
If he tries anything,

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:09.590
my knives will make sure he'll
be leaving with only one eye left!

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:13.010
What's the hold-up? It's very rude to make people wait!

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:15.930
Alright, Joyce!
Open the gate!

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:17.770
Understood!

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.090
That's some hill to climb.

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:51.180
Listen, it'll take some time for me to climb with only one leg.

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:54.460
Unlike you, we are gentlemen.

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:56.930
We'll wait as long as necessary.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:01.580
Really, gentlemen?
That's very kind.

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:02.940
Come on, Puppy, let's go.

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:15.540
The fort will fall! The fort will fall!

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:17.700
They'll all die! They'll all die!
They'll all die!

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:19.940
Wait, Gray!

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:26.750
Don't get worked up.
It's just a stupid parrot.

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:31.300
Flint, be quiet!
You're upsetting our hosts!

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:34.000
They'll all die! They'll all die!

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:37.570
He never listens to me.

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:41.770
Very well, Silver, we're listening.

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:46.730
What? Here? Now?
You're not letting me in?

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:48.020
Of course not!

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:50.700
We don't offer such hospitality to traitors!

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:55.810
I see.
A gentleman must speak honestly.

00:07:56.660 --> 00:08:01.060
I'd rather not sit on the ground,
but I guess I'll have to.

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:03.060
There, I'm sitting.

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:05.860
Someone will have to help me
back up, though.

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:08.130
Hey, Jim!
How's it going?

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:14.260
Seems like you're just fine.
Very much so.

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:16.090
Hey, Puppy.

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:17.380
Yes?

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:18.850
Pass me the bag.

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:19.870
H-Here you go.

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:21.820
Silver, what's in there?

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:24.230
Oh, that you, Dr. Livesey?

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:27.380
Don't worry.
It's nothing dangerous.

00:08:27.380 --> 00:08:32.110
Actually, this morning
I didn't have time to eat.

00:08:32.660 --> 00:08:35.030
I hope you don't mind.

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:40.100
Oh, owner Trelawney.

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:43.220
You look thirsty.
Would you like some coffee?

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:46.830
If you want, there's enough room for two here.

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:50.350
I don't want any!

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:53.930
That's too bad...

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:58.300
Quit playing around, Silver!

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:00.350
Alright.

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:02.810
We'll listen to you.

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:05.520
I want the treasure map.

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:12.290
If you let me have it, I'll let you live.

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:16.780
We outnumber the eight of you
with three to one.

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:19.340
Plus, we are good fighters.

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:22.180
No matter how much you resist,
we will destroy you.

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:24.260
It's only a matter of time.

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:28.800
I don't think that's such a bad deal for you.

00:09:29.340 --> 00:09:32.460
Boy, am I stuffed!
That was delicious.

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:33.760
Hey, Puppy, clean up.

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:34.700
Yes, sir.

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:38.720
I see. Very well.
Let me express our point of view.

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:43.180
If you repent and return our weapons,

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:47.040
we'll promise you a fair trial
when we return to England.

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:49.720
Also, we will do our utmost...

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:52.690
...to keep you from hanging. What do you say?

00:09:56.180 --> 00:09:58.610
Obviously, we won't agree to anything.

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:03.920
This conversation is over! Leave immediately!

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:06.500
The mere sight of you ails me!

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:09.920
One moment, Mr. Smollett.

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:14.820
You don't have a choice and I'll tell you why.

00:10:14.820 --> 00:10:17.890
Take a look at the cliff overlooking the fort.

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:20.340
What?
The cliff?

00:10:25.710 --> 00:10:28.230
A cannon!
When did you bring it up there?!

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:37.110
We've been had!

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:40.070
From up there, they won't
have any trouble hitting us!

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:47.070
Silver!
You dirty rat...

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:49.620
How did you manage to get it up there?

00:10:50.390 --> 00:10:53.110
It took all night, with all of us.

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:55.670
Thanks to you, I had three injured to carry.

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:58.340
The distance from the ship was very far,

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:00.540
so I didn't want to waste our powder.

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:04.790
Well now, give me that map.

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:07.180
Otherwise, you'll be destroyed along with the fort!

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:19.150
I would've liked an immediate response,

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:24.330
but I'm also a gentlemen.
I'll give you until nightfall.

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:35.120
What a sight I am.

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:39.410
Because I've been sitting for too long,
my one leg's gone numb.

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:41.130
Hey, Jim!

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:43.490
I'm stuck, give me a hand!

00:11:47.590 --> 00:11:51.520
We got along so well before... Makes me sad.

00:11:56.390 --> 00:11:58.820
They'll all die! They'll all die!

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:03.660
They'll all die! They'll all die!
They'll all die!

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:20.170
We can't give them the map!

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:26.850
If we don't, we'll be reduced to a pulp by nightfall!

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:31.770
Let them fire if they want to!

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:35.560
I refuse to give in to this band of pirates!

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:39.160
I refuse to surrender to the threats of Silver!

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:43.990
Captain!
There's no need to shout like that!

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:46.320
But if we are going to,
I can shout louder!

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:49.460
Therefore, I have an idea!

00:12:50.460 --> 00:12:52.960
Ben Gunn can get us out of here.

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:54.130
Ben Gunn?

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:54.130
Ben Gunn?

00:12:57.580 --> 00:13:01.590
What do you say, Jim?
You think you can find him?

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:03.010
Y-Yes, sir.

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:05.550
If I can get out of here,
I think I can...

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:10.460
You said he knew the island like the back of his hand, right?

00:13:10.460 --> 00:13:12.060
Y-Yes.

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:13.520
I want you to ask him,

00:13:14.340 --> 00:13:19.190
"Is there a place on this island where the seven of us can take refuge?"

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:21.940
"A place where our inferior numbers...

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:25.150
...aren't a disadvantage in combat?"

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:28.620
A cave, for example.

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:30.470
What do you say, gentlemen?

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:34.340
We mustn't give in to Silver's threats no matter what.

00:13:34.340 --> 00:13:38.580
What we must do now is leave
this fort and find a new shelter.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:42.550
Yes, Captain.
That's a brilliant idea!

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:46.930
Jim, I'll get out of the fort ahead of you.

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:50.350
I'll distract them, and you run.

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:53.270
Go straight.
Don't look back.

00:13:54.440 --> 00:13:55.510
Can you make it, Jim?

00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:56.230
Aye.

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:57.730
If you don't find him...

00:13:58.420 --> 00:14:01.220
...and night has fallen,
don't come back here.

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:05.360
Silver always keeps his word.
So don't risk your life.

00:14:07.840 --> 00:14:09.970
Joyce, Hunter, lend me a hand.

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:10.600
Sure thing.

00:14:09.970 --> 00:14:11.330
Good, let's go.

00:14:12.480 --> 00:14:13.450
OK!

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:14.650
I'm going!

00:14:20.140 --> 00:14:21.500
It's that traitor, Gray!

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:22.800
Fire!

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:27.130
Don't let him get away!

00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:28.880
Hold it!

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:31.180
Wait!

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:34.310
Alright, now!

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:36.370
OK!

00:14:39.040 --> 00:14:40.180
Go on, Jim!

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:07.340
Go, grab 'im.
His musket is empty!

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:22.060
Come on, whoever wants to taste my blade, step forward.

00:15:25.170 --> 00:15:26.360
Dammit...

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:27.980
Get 'em! Get 'em!

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:33.240
Joyce! Joyce!

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:36.160
Grab on!

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:40.370
Filthy dog!

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:49.760
Joyce, what about Jim?
Did he make it?

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:53.010
All went well. He's gone into the forest! We did it!

00:15:59.240 --> 00:16:02.440
Joyce, hang on!
Hey, Joyce!

00:16:03.280 --> 00:16:04.690
Joyce, borther, what is it?

00:16:15.080 --> 00:16:17.400
Ben Gunn!

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:18.740
Hey!

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:20.700
Ben Gunn!

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:24.670
Hey, Ben Gunn, where are you?

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:26.690
I saw him...

00:16:27.490 --> 00:16:32.220
Th-That brave Jim...
He ran straight for the woods!

00:16:32.440 --> 00:16:35.720
Do you remember, Hunter?
When we were kids,

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:39.270
we ran with all our might, like Jim did.

00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:43.960
Straight ahead...
No matter how far.

00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:46.030
No matter how long...

00:16:56.060 --> 00:16:57.010
Dear brother!

00:16:57.310 --> 00:16:59.070
BROTHER!

00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:12.590
Ben Gunn, show yourself!
It's me, Jim!

00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:24.030
BEN GUNN!

00:17:27.890 --> 00:17:30.320
What's it look like?
Any movement in the fort?

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:32.820
No, nothing to report.

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:37.820
Very well, then we'll proceed
with the next phase of our plan.

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:38.780
Alright.

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:49.040
BEN GUNN!

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:51.960
Ben Gunn! Ben Gunn! Ben GUNN!

00:17:54.160 --> 00:17:56.010
The sun will set soon.

00:17:56.440 --> 00:17:59.470
Looks like Jim couldn't find Ben Gunn.

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:02.160
In that case, we must decide. What should we do?

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:05.590
If we stay here, we'll be like
sitting ducks for that cannon.

00:18:05.590 --> 00:18:09.110
We must take our chances and leave the fort.

00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:21.000
Benbow, we're gonna return to the fort!

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:23.250
We have to fight alongside the others!

00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:41.220
The cannon!

00:18:41.220 --> 00:18:42.660
I see...

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:45.830
I must've made a turn without realizing it!

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:53.240
That's weird.

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:56.360
Why aren't any of Silver's men guarding the cannon?

00:19:04.420 --> 00:19:05.370
That's dirty!

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:11.880
It's a fake, this cannon!
A piece of wood covered with tar!

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:12.670
We fell for—

00:19:14.480 --> 00:19:16.610
Okay... we'll see about that!

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:23.100
Mr. Trelawney, you haven't forgotten anything?

00:19:23.100 --> 00:19:25.000
No, n-nothing!

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:27.040
Alright, listen everyone!

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:29.560
They're going to fire soon.

00:19:29.560 --> 00:19:32.480
There will be a lot of smoke.

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:33.990
That'll be our chance.

00:19:33.990 --> 00:19:36.880
We'll leave at the same time,
then split up.

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:37.900
We'll meet at—

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:39.170
One moment, Captain.

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:43.030
Fellows, look up there.

00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:54.630
It's Jim!
Could that really be him?

00:20:01.480 --> 00:20:02.880
Yes, I did it!

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:06.140
That'll teach you to play dirty tricks, Silver!

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:13.950
I knew they would figure it out sooner or later...

00:20:16.680 --> 00:20:19.150
Very well!
Move to the next phase!

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:37.920
Those screams...!
Damn it!

00:20:38.360 --> 00:20:41.020
Silver and his men are attacking! Hurry, Benbow!

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:43.760
They're here!
To the main gate!

00:20:55.120 --> 00:20:57.200
Captain Smollett, something's wrong!

00:20:57.760 --> 00:20:59.980
We can hear their screams,
but no one's in sight!

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:01.510
What?

00:21:07.480 --> 00:21:08.490
What are you doing?!

00:21:09.280 --> 00:21:10.700
Don't move from there!

00:21:13.600 --> 00:21:15.670
What did you drop in the well?!

00:21:16.160 --> 00:21:17.210
Nothing.

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:19.300
Answer me!

00:21:43.480 --> 00:21:44.780
Now they've done it!

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:46.300
Where are they? Where?!
Tell me where!

00:21:46.800 --> 00:21:48.590
Where are Silver's men?!

00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:51.660
C-Captain Smollett!

00:22:12.790 --> 00:22:14.390
Captain Silver, we did it.

00:22:14.390 --> 00:22:17.320
Good, you reached the well?

00:22:17.920 --> 00:22:20.670
My diversion tactic wasn't that bad.

00:22:28.570 --> 00:22:32.370
To      be        continued

00:22:33.420 --> 00:22:38.460
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:33.420 --> 00:22:38.460
Hey sea breeze

00:22:38.460 --> 00:22:44.270
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:38.460 --> 00:22:44.270
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:45.490 --> 00:22:50.480
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:45.490 --> 00:22:50.480
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:55.920
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:55.920
A word to my dear mother

00:22:55.920 --> 00:23:01.480
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:55.920 --> 00:23:01.480
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:23:01.480 --> 00:23:06.940
kaban ippai no

00:23:01.480 --> 00:23:06.940
And that my bag filled

00:23:06.940 --> 00:23:12.570
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:06.940 --> 00:23:12.570
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:12.570 --> 00:23:18.430
kakaete kaeritai

00:23:12.570 --> 00:23:18.430
Will be brought back

00:23:19.520 --> 00:23:25.120
yuuyake wo senaka ni

00:23:19.520 --> 00:23:25.120
The sunset on my back

00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:31.010
kamome wo kata ni tomarasete

00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:31.010
And a seagull perched on my shoulder

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:40.730
boku wa fukimasu kuchibue wo

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:40.730
I blow out a whistle

00:23:45.400 --> 00:23:49.920
It's terrible! The pirates have poisoned the fort's well!

00:23:49.920 --> 00:23:52.070
We need clear water to save the captain.

00:23:52.070 --> 00:23:56.130
Dammit, how dare they to do this?
They really are merciless!

00:23:56.130 --> 00:23:57.830
But I refuse to admit defeat.

00:23:57.830 --> 00:24:02.230
I'm going to dig a tunnel to get out of the fort and get to the river!

00:24:02.230 --> 00:24:05.580
But, on the other side awaits...!

00:24:05.580 --> 00:24:08.630
Next time on Treasure Island:
"Surrender, Silver-Style"

00:24:08.640 --> 00:24:13.640
m 0 0 l 960 0 960 720 0 720

00:24:08.640 --> 00:24:13.640
*

00:24:08.640 --> 00:24:13.640
Next time

00:24:08.640 --> 00:24:13.640
Coming soon!

00:24:08.640 --> 00:24:13.640
Surrender, Silver-Style

00:24:08.920 --> 00:24:10.300
It's war!
